			<div class="content" id="post-content-2206938">
									

<p>Why is this thing housed in plexiglass? even thick plexiglass?</p>
<p>It COMPELS people who see it to lay their hands upon the bar, triggering it's effect. It should be housed in an OPAQUE container. Basically, any crate/steel box big enough to hold it.</p>
<p>Other than that, the concept is acceptable.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">so, if the pusher/victim of the SCP dies within 2 hours, the &quot;baby&quot; vanishes, and the carriage degrades within 30 minutes?<br /></span>if they last for 2 hours, the baby attacks, eating them, and &#8230; presumably goes on a rampage.</p>
<p>I REALLY wonder about the origins of this one. :D</p>

